WEBVTT

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.120
Wait...

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:16.720
What did he say to me that time?

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:25.330
Atsushi, I'll buy you a cake afterwards.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.180
Oh, you're a good boy, Atsushi.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:53.630
What... was he saying?

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:56.050
Young master!

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:59.360
I can't fry the eggs properly!

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:00.470
I got it!

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:03.680
I got it, so turn off the stove till I get out.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:09.230
Yay!

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:11.150
Just as I expected, yours taste good.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:14.110
Didn't we have fried eggs yesterday too?

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:16.440
This is really delicious.

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:20.760
What is it, young master?

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:22.070
Nothing.

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:29.790
I was just thinking about how often your insensitivity to my feelings has saved me.

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:32.130
Yes. Thank you very much!

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:00.420
Oh, this is a new one.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:02.760
It's a cake called Anja.

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:08.470
I combined a sweet-and-sour rhubarb tart with raspberry mousse.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:20.650
Sensei, I really like this!

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:23.880
The mousse and rhubarb are really well matched.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:27.770
Isn't this the kind of cake you like, Kanda-kun?

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:29.900
By the way, Eiji.

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:32.040
What?

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:36.080
We've decided to sell your new chiboust.

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:46.430
Finally, I feel gramps is prostrating himself before my mastery.

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:48.050
What?!

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:50.850
Wouldn't it be common sense to thank me?!

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:53.730
Kanda-kun is just a bit self-conscious.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.310
Let's open up. Open up!

00:04:58.310 --> 00:04:59.290
Yes!

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.280
Right!

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:05.300
Welcome.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:06.640
Good morning.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:08.240
What do you recommend today?

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:11.780
Then, how about our new Anja?

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:19.960
A marriage of a rhubarb tart containing sweet compote that will melt on the tongue, with a sweet-and-sour raspberry mousse.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:21.710
Well then, I'll try it.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:25.250
Do you want three pieces, as usual?

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:26.010
Yes.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.600
Thank you very much.

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:31.940
Umm...

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:37.470
Yes, welcome.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:38.730
What would you like?

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:40.590
No.

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:43.500
My name is Ono Nagako.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:47.450
I heard that my brother is working here.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:51.580
Nagako?

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:55.550
Yeah. I said I don't mind,

00:05:55.550 --> 00:05:57.620
but she said she could wait till your break.

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:00.080
She said she'll be waiting here.

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:04.090
I didn't know you had such a beautiful sister.

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:06.380
Why didn't you introduce her to me?

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:11.360
How could I introduce her? I haven't even seen her for almost ten years.

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:16.910
I haven't been back to my parents' house since I came out as a gay.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:17.790
Is that so?

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:21.490
I had other issues with my mother as well.

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:25.890
It happened in my second year of middle school.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:31.470
My mother and my teacher were in my parents' bedroom.

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:36.070
And he was...

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:39.060
the first man I fell in love with.

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:44.800
Eiji, is it all right for Ono to leave now?

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:47.050
Yeah, no problem.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:48.830
Tachibana...

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:50.350
Go.

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:51.930
Your sister is waiting.

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:02.020
Nine?

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:04.820
No, I guess it's been ten years.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:08.080
But you haven't changed at all.

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:09.490
That surprised me.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:14.110
I'm surprised you're so big.

00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:15.780
Of course.

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:18.930
You haven't seen me since I was in middle school.

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:21.360
I'm already 24.

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:24.190
You're a lot like Mom when she was young.

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:26.370
Only in appearance.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:30.840
I heard you're working at a company that publishes children's books.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:32.100
Yup.

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:36.180
I'm a normal office worker,

00:07:37.130 --> 00:07:39.890
and I'm going to have a normal marriage with a colleague.

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:46.580
And if it's at all possible, I'd like the entire family to attend the wedding ceremony.

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:49.160
You really still don't want to see...

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:50.650
Mom and Dad?

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:55.500
No, it's not like I don't want to see them.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:57.590
Rather,

00:07:57.590 --> 00:08:01.190
wouldn't it be a problem for someone like me to attend?

00:08:01.190 --> 00:08:02.740
Onii-chan...

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:07.340
Did you know that Dad had other women besides Mom?

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:10.800
So you didn't know?

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:12.100
Yeah.

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:13.670
I see.

00:08:13.670 --> 00:08:16.950
I thought you knew as well.

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:19.840
Do you...

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:21.290
know about Mom?

00:08:23.570 --> 00:08:24.930
No, it's nothing.

00:08:26.350 --> 00:08:29.770
S-So Dad had....

00:08:29.770 --> 00:08:33.340
He was so kind and sincere.

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:38.840
Even though we have a lot of problems, we're still a family.

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:41.940
I was hoping we could get together once again.

00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:43.750
So I...

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:45.710
Nagako...

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:51.670
You don't have to decide now.

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:53.630
Okay.

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:57.350
Anyway, I'm sorry that I'm late in telling you this...

00:08:58.160 --> 00:08:59.380
Congratulations.

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:01.230
I'm happy for you.

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:03.020
Really, I'm happy.

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:13.940
O-no-kun!

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:18.800
Hey, why did your sister make a fleeting appearance here?

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:21.130
Well, she's going to get married.

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:28.760
Sensei, congratulations!

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:29.780
Thanks.

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:40.800
Here's your tea.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:44.180
And there's milk in your son's.

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:53.570
Now, eat it, Atsushi.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:55.140
Hey.

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:59.030
I'm thinking of closing my shop and going back to Sendai.

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:03.240
My brother's family is running a shop there.

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:08.310
I'm considering helping them and taking things easy.

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:09.170
So...

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:12.210
Atsushi, is it good?

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:14.170
Won't you come with me?

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:17.140
Oh! Don't spill it.

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:19.630
Your manners are so poor.

00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:23.100
You won't have to worry about money.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:25.810
I've saved a bit.

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:28.130
Now, now, you're spilling it again.

00:10:28.130 --> 00:10:30.510
You're a bad boy.

00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:33.400
Hey, Sendai is a really good place.

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:35.700
Now, now, you're a good boy.

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:37.430
You can have mine too.

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:41.760
You have some on your cheek.

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:43.780
There.

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:46.780
I see. Is it tasty?

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:51.540
I'm really happy when you say it's tasty.

00:10:54.190 --> 00:10:55.670
You poor thing.

00:10:57.820 --> 00:10:58.550
Don't touch me.

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:00.340
But...

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:04.250
Isn't it tasty, Atsushi?

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:07.750
It's nothing, nothing.

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:09.580
Isn't it tasty?

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:11.350
Atsushi, isn't it tasty?

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:15.440
As long as you're here, I don't need anything else.

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:17.290
Stop it!

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:21.320
Your son died twenty years ago!

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:34.950
Shut up.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:38.910
Please...

00:11:38.910 --> 00:11:40.530
come with me.

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:41.260
Hey...

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:55.490
Please come with me.

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:09.460
Not again.

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:16.480
Young master!

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:18.320
The eggs...

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:21.980
Déjà vu.

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:31.930
By the way, isn't it strange for two grown men to face each other over breakfast every day?

00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:34.790
We're like a gay married couple.

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:37.670
That bastard Eiji!

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:40.440
Teaching you to say something like that!

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:43.990
The missing boy is nine year old Daiki-kun,

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:47.320
the first son of Kamei Masahiro, an office worker living in Suginami-ku, Tokyo.

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:51.180
According to our information,

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:55.880
Daiki-kun was apparently kidnapped on his way back home from cram school on the 16th, at 10PM.

00:12:55.880 --> 00:13:01.300
The police are investigating the case on the assumption that Daiki-kun may have been kidnapped.

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:03.330
Poor boy.

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:08.010
He's the same age as you were when you were kidnapped.

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:14.480
Your insensitivity has really saved me, seriously.

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:17.340
Yes. Thank you very much!

00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:28.920
You're putting in too much sugar.

00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:30.860
Your blood-sugar levels will rise.

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:32.780
What are you talking about, Yoshioka?

00:13:32.780 --> 00:13:36.920
This is diet sweetener with half the calories.

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:40.010
But if you use two, there's no difference.

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:42.380
Oh, by the way,

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:47.470
I heard they're setting up a unified investigation headquarters here.

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:48.610
Yeah.

00:13:48.610 --> 00:13:50.470
That's because none of the incidents have been solved.

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:55.100
They think the same kidnapper is involved in all the cases so far.

00:13:55.940 --> 00:13:57.310
The same kidnapper...

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:04.450
Well, the victims have all been small children.

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:09.450
The method of murder is always the same, strangulation, but that's not definitive.

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:14.620
Oddly, the stomach contents of all the victims were similar.

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:16.830
The stomach contents?

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:18.320
Yeah.

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:22.890
None of the dead bodies contained what you would call "normal" food.

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:28.010
Instead, things like biscuits, dairy products, chocolate.

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:30.890
Does that mean that the kidnapper only fed them snacks?

00:14:31.190 --> 00:14:32.180
No.

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:34.580
Fruit was also found,

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:39.230
but unusual fruit that's only sold in upscale supermarkets.

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:41.850
And each body contained only a little bit.

00:14:43.310 --> 00:14:48.900
In short, all of that put together might be just enough to make a cake.

00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:50.450
What do you mean?

00:14:51.190 --> 00:14:56.970
Come to think of it, I investigated a kidnapping similar to this more than twenty years ago.

00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:02.960
I was saddled with an unpleasant boss, and the case ended up going nowhere.

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:12.050
Well, this might be our sole remaining hope.

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:16.640
I know that I'm intruding, but a boy's life is in danger.

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:18.430
So, how about it?

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:22.440
Is a cake made with those ingredients unusual?

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:25.100
Raspberry, fresh cream,

00:15:25.100 --> 00:15:29.770
powdered almond, rhubarb, cerfeuil...

00:15:29.770 --> 00:15:35.620
Rhubarb is a vegetable like butterbur, sold at upscale supermarkets.

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:36.770
Yes.

00:15:36.770 --> 00:15:41.150
It's a very sour vegetable, mainly eaten in Europe.

00:15:41.150 --> 00:15:44.600
Usually it's made into compote as an ingredient in cakes or jam.

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:51.550
Cerfeuil has no taste or smell, and it's often put on a cake to enhance the color.

00:15:52.860 --> 00:15:55.850
These days, a few shops use rhubarb.

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:59.350
Many more shops use cerfeuil.

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:02.770
The other ingredients are commonplace, too.

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:05.920
I see.

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:09.650
So it's impossible to identify the shop from the ingredients.

00:16:10.770 --> 00:16:12.380
But...

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:16.060
when you consider the combination of ingredients, it's a different matter.

00:16:16.630 --> 00:16:17.640
You mean...

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:23.060
Normally, rhubarb is used alone in tarts or cakes.

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:26.500
But, in this cake, it's been combined with raspberry mousse,

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:31.380
and the base is probably a tart with almond cream.

00:16:31.830 --> 00:16:35.550
A cake shop in Tokyo that uses rhubarb like this...

00:16:35.910 --> 00:16:38.600
I only know of one.

00:16:39.810 --> 00:16:41.060
One?

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:43.730
Antique.

00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:46.540
Thank you very much.

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:49.350
Thank you very much.

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:55.610
Welcome, Akutagawa-sama.

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:57.990
Thank you very much for your patronage.

00:16:57.990 --> 00:17:00.200
Is it closing time?

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:02.490
Please don't mind about that.

00:17:02.490 --> 00:17:06.830
Did you like the Anja you bought last time?

00:17:07.150 --> 00:17:08.220
Yeah.

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:17.590
I-Is it Ono? Are you looking for Ono?

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:21.600
Two men fighting over Ono in Ni-chome...

00:17:21.960 --> 00:17:23.350
Or is it Eiji?

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:25.730
Did he kick someone to death?

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:27.110
Oh, no, no, no, no.

00:17:27.110 --> 00:17:28.240
It's not like that.

00:17:28.240 --> 00:17:34.190
We came here to ask if you could help us on a case we're investigating now.

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:37.780
I see.

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:40.030
Then please say that sooner.

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:42.000
A-Akutagawa-san.

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:45.530
Is this flippant man that...

00:17:45.530 --> 00:17:48.090
He's <i>that</i> Tachibana Keiichirou-kun.

00:17:58.550 --> 00:17:59.710
What's going on?

00:17:59.710 --> 00:18:00.810
No idea.

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:04.860
Our cake...

00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:05.600
Yeah.

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:09.310
We already had your cake examined by the Forensics Section.

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:14.860
And the ingredients were the same as the contents of the victims' stomachs.

00:18:20.350 --> 00:18:24.110
The kidnapper has probably appeared here twice, maybe three times.

00:18:24.110 --> 00:18:27.330
And now a fourth child is missing.

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:30.020
There isn't a moment to lose.

00:18:30.020 --> 00:18:33.440
We want to bring this child, at least, home safely.

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:35.550
Like you.

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:38.010
Wasn't...

00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:45.470
Wasn't I waiting for this day?

00:18:46.990 --> 00:18:49.090
I wanted to make this shop small...

00:18:49.550 --> 00:18:53.060
so I could see what was going on everywhere.

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:56.920
And to stay open as long as possible.

00:18:57.680 --> 00:19:04.370
A shop where people of any occupation, age, or sex would buy cake without hesitation.

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:08.080
The reason I wanted to make the shop like that was...

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:10.680
all for this day...

00:19:13.280 --> 00:19:17.240
I'm really sorry for what I put you and your family through.

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:20.800
Akutagawa-san,

00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:25.210
you were the only one who said to consider every possibility,

00:19:25.210 --> 00:19:30.600
and to investigate every suspicious person in the area.

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:33.960
But we didn't listen to you.

00:19:33.960 --> 00:19:41.730
We ignored your opinion, considering you a young, bossy upstart who didn't know what was really going on.

00:19:42.690 --> 00:19:45.600
We jumped to the conclusion that this was a kidnapping for ransom.

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:49.200
And that caused us to delay the start of the investigation.

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:51.400
It was inexcusable.

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:56.160
I know that this won't change anything, but please let me apologize.

00:19:56.160 --> 00:20:00.440
I didn't say that because I had any real evidence.

00:20:01.020 --> 00:20:04.800
I was a policeman without any experience,

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:07.430
and all I really knew how to do was to go by the book.

00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:13.950
I didn't stick to my guns after being laughed at.

00:20:14.760 --> 00:20:20.780
If I'd investigated as though it had been my child who'd been kidnapped...

00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:24.110
In that way, I'm equally to blame.

00:20:24.830 --> 00:20:26.160
Akutagawa-san...

00:20:28.880 --> 00:20:34.660
There isn't anyone who can take full responsibility for his actions.

00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:51.210
It makes me want to puke!

00:20:51.210 --> 00:20:51.930
Die, you homo!

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:21.980
Fine.

00:21:21.980 --> 00:21:24.970
It will be my pleasure to help your investigation.
